// @reject: a loop specifier is a count (Int) or a condition (Bool). An array is
// @reject: neither, and reading it through truthiness meant guessing: the
// @reject: tree-walker called it false, the VM called it true, zyml refused it.
// @reject: Three answers to one question is not a language feature.
items = [1, 2, 3]
@ items {
    >> "x" ¶
}
